{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:22:50.536Z","tool_name":"update_topic","tool_id":"update_topic__call_188592","parameters":{"strategic_intent":"Investigate and implement Iteration 6: smoothed 336-slot direct CRPS forward calibration, asymmetric leverage effect (negative return volatility response), and OHLC Parkinson range blending.","summary":"Iteration 5 improved 35 out of 36 asset-window cells over Iteration 4 and all 6 competition-window totals. Now in Iteration 6, I am investigating three structural refinements on pre-validation data: (1) replacing the piecewise-constant 10-session forward multiplier with a smooth empirical-Bayes 336-slot CRPS-optimal forward multiplier table; (2) incorporating the GJR-GARCH asymmetric volatility (leverage) effect where negative recent returns induce higher future volatility than positive returns of equal magnitude; and (3) blending scale-anchored OHLC Parkinson range into the short-scale EWMAs.","title":"Iteration 6: Smooth 336-Slot CRPS Calibration, Asymmetric Leverage & OHLC Range"}}
{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:22:50.974Z","tool_id":"update_topic__call_188592","status":"success","output":"## 📂 Topic: **Iteration 6: Smooth 336-Slot CRPS Calibration, Asymmetric Leverage & OHLC Range**\n\n**Summary:**\nIteration 5 improved 35 out of 36 asset-window cells over Iteration 4 and all 6 competition-window totals. Now in Iteration 6, I am investigating three structural refinements on pre-validation data: (1) replacing the piecewise-constant 10-session forward multiplier with a smooth empirical-Bayes 336-slot CRPS-optimal forward multiplier table; (2) incorporating the GJR-GARCH asymmetric volatility (leverage) effect where negative recent returns induce higher future volatility than positive returns of equal magnitude; and (3) blending scale-anchored OHLC Parkinson range into the short-scale EWMAs.\n\n> [!STRATEGY]\n> **Intent:** Investigate and implement Iteration 6: smoothed 336-slot direct CRPS forward calibration, asymmetric leverage effect (negative return volatility response), and OHLC Parkinson range blending."}
